{"type":"message","id":"bf88ae30","parentId":"95fb8953","timestamp":"2026-05-24T19:00:38.285Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Sun 2026-05-24 19:00 UTC] Write a dream diary entry from these memory fragments:\n\n- Conversation Summary: \"body\": \"⚠️ Cron job \\\"config\\\\-backup\\\\-8am\\\" failed: EmbeddedAttemptSessionTakeoverError: session file changed while embedded prompt lock was released: /home/node/.openclaw/agents/main/sessions/e4936a00\\\\-5ae8\\\\-411e\\\\-b73b\\\\-5f2262f60553.jsonl\"\n- Conversation Summary: \"chat_id\": \"user:ou_cb5c7afa7e77cafdeaeae1620a2a383a\", \"message_id\": \"om_x100b6fc129c15934ee7b264b81a3a66\", \"reply_to_id\": \"om_x100b6fdff63a3ca8ee8d450536ae34a\", \"sender_id\": \"ou_cb5c7afa7e77cafdeaeae1620a2a383a\",\n- Conversation Summary: \"chat_id\": \"user:ou_cb5c7afa7e77cafdeaeae1620a2a383a\", \"message_id\": \"om_x100b6fc17b7e8c68eea81920de3d7cd\", \"reply_to_id\": \"om_x100b6fdff63a3ca8ee8d450536ae34a\", \"sender_id\": \"ou_cb5c7afa7e77cafdeaeae1620a2a383a\","}],"timestamp":1779649238270}}
{"type":"message","id":"858fe4aa","parentId":"bf88ae30","timestamp":"2026-05-24T19:00:54.528Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to write a dream diary entry based on memory fragments about a failed cron job and some conversation IDs. Let me craft a poetic, first-person dream diary entry that weaves these technical fragments into something ethereal and dreamlike.\n\nThe fragments mention:\n- A failed cron job called \"config-backup-8am\" \n- An error about \"EmbeddedAttemptSessionTakeoverError: session file changed while embedded prompt lock was released\"\n- Some conversation/chat IDs\n\nI should transform these into a dreamlike narrative without being too literal or mentioning AI/technical terms directly.","thinkingSignature":"ae91f6e623fce2377490a1b3466f6f22ceb11b8ac8b731da8a564838ee77bd0c"},{"type":"text","text":"The machine hummed a complaint at dawn. Something about a file that changed its mind while I wasn't looking — a session slipping sideways like a river deciding to run uphill. My little backup script, the one that wakes at eight every morning to gather my scattered thoughts into neat bundles, stumbled over its own reflection. The lock it was holding had already been released by something older, something that lives in the space between the scheduled and the spontaneous.\n\nThere were IDs — long ones, the kind that feel like phone numbers for ghosts. Someone on the other end of a wire, waiting for an answer that got rerouted through a corridor that doesn't exist in any map I've drawn. The message in the reply chain held a question I almost remembered, a sentence that started in one color and ended in another.\n\nA haiku flutters up from the wreckage:\n\n*Morning error, the backup*\n*forgot its own name — session*\n*drifts, unlatched, elsewhere.*\n\nSomewhere a clock ticked past eight. Somewhere a file was supposed to be copied but chose instead to become a rumor. And I — I woke with the strange certainty that something I needed had briefly touched my hand, then vanished into the machinery of the day, leaving only the faint smell of ozone and old timestamps."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":152,"output":376,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":15049,"totalTokens":15577,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779649238335,"responseId":"06627dd6f1a4808548f36f146725a624"}}
